Z||000000||yellowFormula||05-23-99||07:52 PM||||Has anyone installed a turbo charger for a v6 , either the one from IRM or any other one,if so I would like some info on it, like was it worth it and how much did you pay for it etc. etc.
Z||000001||Eric||05-23-99||08:43 PM||||I was thinking of installing a turbo on my V6 after I did my 3.1 rebuild (either that or NOS).  The concept behind the turbo is quite simple and can be employed on almost any car.  I was thinking of using a donor turbo from a junked car because it's more cost effective than some of the kits on the market (around $4000).  The most difficult thing is adapting the stock exaust to fit the turbo (easy if you're a good welder).  Overall I think the turbo can be a worthwile  modification.<p>You should consider a rebuild before you attempt to bolt on a turbo or even NOS for that matter.  The stock pistons on the V6 cannot handle the 200+ horsepower a turbo will provide.  As an alternative to turbo you may want to consider a 3.1 rebuild.  I'm sure you have heard of this before, but it is a reliable means of achieving over 200 horsepower and for about the same cost of a junk turbo with no rebuild.  And there is NO LAG! If you want to know more about this check out 3.1 build over in the general fiero chat.  I am going to be starting my rebuild in the next month or so and will answer any question you might have about this.  Good luck.
